                                "text": "I don’t have a problem with gardeners controlling ivy where it may be considered a weed; those who like tidy gardens keeping it at bay through cutting (I’ll leave ‘tidy’ gardening to another post!). The big problem arises when people who are used to controlling ivy in these contexts develop a sort of vendetta against the plant, and extend their gardening ethic to the surrounding countryside."
